<section class="card">
    <h1>FileDrop Help</h1>
    <p class="muted">Use FileDrop when files are too large or too sensitive to send as normal email attachments.</p>

    <div class="help-grid">
        <div>
            <h2>Sending Files</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>Click <strong>New Transfer</strong>.</li>
                <li>Enter the recipient's email address.</li>
                <li>Add an optional subject and message.</li>
                <li>Choose an expiration date up to 30 days.</li>
                <li>Drag files into the upload box or browse to select them.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Upload Files</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Receiving Files</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>Open the FileDrop email.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Download Files</strong>.</li>
                <li>Download individual files from the secure page.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Best Practices</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Use short expiration periods when possible.</li>
                <li>Confirm the recipient email before sending.</li>
                <li>Use ZIP files for folders or large groups of files.</li>
                <li>Do not share download links publicly.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Administration</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Use the Admin dashboard to view transfers.</li>
                <li>Use Audit Log to review system activity.</li>
                <li>Use Health to confirm database, storage, and email status.</li>
                <li>Use Settings to adjust retention defaults.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
